--- /dev/null+++ b/ION/05_context/current/audited_read_action_quarantine_membrane_context_package/ION_AUDITED_READ_ACTION_QUARANTINE_MEMBRANE_v0_1/protocols/AUDITED_READ_PROTOCOL.md@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@+# AUDITED_READ_PROTOCOL
+
+Status: `CANDIDATE_NOT_ACCEPTED`
+
+## Law
+
+Every successful or refused read-like operation over allowed local/project state MUST emit an audit event.
+
+Read-like operations include:
+
+- `file_read`
+- `file_search`
+- `tree_list`
+- `registry_read`
+- `receipt_search`
+- `queue_status`
+- `runner_status`
+- `git_status_summary`
+- `artifact_manifest`
+- `context_compile`
+- extension queue/status projections
+
+## What to log
+
+The audit event MUST record:
+
+- actor/callsign/carrier
+- tool/surface used
+- target paths or roots
+- operation intent/purpose
+- authority flags
+- result status
+- bytes/mtime/hash if available
+- redaction policy
+- whether content was logged
+
+## What not to log
+
+The read ledger MUST NOT store raw secret contents. For sensitive surfaces, log:
+
+```text
+event_type: read_refused
+reason: secret_or_forbidden_surface
+content_logged: false
+```
+
+## Allowed read posture
+
+A read being allowed does not imply write authority or accepted-state authority.
